;; The facade containers connect to their shell bridge's Unix socket (the
;; general and the personal bridge are the same program in the same domain).
;;
;; For AF_UNIX the `connectto` check compares the *creating process's* domain,
;; not the socket file's label: each bridge runs as the unconfined system service
;; (`unconfined_service_t`), a facade container is `container_t:s0:cX,cY`, and
;; the relabel that `:z` applies to the file changes nothing about the socket's
;; security ID. Without this rule every connect() is EACCES at the inode that
;; looks perfectly accessible -- 0660 on the bridge's group -- and `shell.run`
;; fails as if the socket were broken.
;;
;; The surface is one domain pair and one socket class: no file, process or
;; network permission is widened, and a container still reaches the socket only
;; if the socket is mounted into it.
(allow container_t unconfined_service_t (unix_stream_socket (connectto getattr getopt read write shutdown)))
(allow unconfined_service_t container_t (unix_stream_socket (getattr getopt read write sendto recvfrom shutdown)))
